WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.680
Martin Scorsese's 2010 feature "Shutter&nbsp;
Island" is a gripping psychological thriller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:11.280
with one twist after another. It's also the second&nbsp;
highest-grossing movie of the director's career.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.760
At first, the film appears to tell the story of&nbsp;
Teddy Daniels. He's a U.S. Marshal investigating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.560
the disappearance of a patient named Rachel&nbsp;
Solando from a mental hospital located on Shutter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.920
Island, an isolated outpost in Boston Harbor. For&nbsp;
this case, Teddy is working with his new partner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:30.400
Chuck Aule. While at the hospital, Teddy&nbsp;
begins experiencing hallucinations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:35.600
nightmares and migraines; everything is&nbsp;
strangely off in a way he doesn't understand.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:40.960
He goes deeper and deeper down a rabbit hole of&nbsp;
madness until he finally confronts Dr. Cawley,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.520
who runs the Shutter Island facility. Cawley&nbsp;
explains to him that he's not really Teddy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:50.640
Daniels; instead, he's Andrew Laeddis, a&nbsp;
traumatized man who killed his wife after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.240
she drowned their three children. The&nbsp;
disappearance Teddy believes he's been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:59.520
investigating has actually been an experimental&nbsp;
treatment to cure him of his manic delusions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.240
The Shutter Island doctors hope that by&nbsp;
indulging Laeddis' belief he is Teddy Daniels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:08.320
he'll be able to come to the conclusion&nbsp;
on his own about what really happened and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:12.960
accept what he did. Throughout this treatment,&nbsp;
the hospital staff has been participating in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:18.400
the elaborate charade, and Chuck, Teddy's&nbsp;
supposed partner, isn't even a U.S. Marshall.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:25.840
"Don't you recognize me, Andrew? I've been your&nbsp;
primary psychiatrist for the last two years."

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.880
One of the great things about&nbsp;
"Shutter Island" is that it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:34.480
a very different experience watching the movie&nbsp;
with knowledge of the twist versus not knowing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:39.840
The second time watching it, you can see all the&nbsp;
ways Scorsese hints at what's really happening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:44.480
before it's revealed. In fact, there are subtle&nbsp;
clues in the first few minutes of the film.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:47.920
While taking the ferry to Shutter Island,&nbsp;
Teddy is throwing up in the bathroom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.480
which he thinks is because he's seasick.&nbsp;
Actually, it's because he's withdrawing from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:56.640
his medication and the ocean reminds him of the&nbsp;
water in which his wife drowned their children.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.240
Then he goes up to the deck and&nbsp;
meets Chuck, his new partner.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:03.280
Teddy doesn't seem to think it's weird&nbsp;
that he's meeting him for the first time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.800
on deck. Logically they would&nbsp;
have gotten on the ferry together.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:11.200
Since the film doesn't make a point of underlining&nbsp;
how strange Teddy and Chuck's introduction is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.880
it's easy to accept it as a normal event.&nbsp;
But it's the first bit of foreshadowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:19.920
that things are not what they seem at Shutter&nbsp;
Island and something is very off with Teddy.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:23.360
There are other intriguing hints about&nbsp;
the "Shutter Island" twist contained in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.600
the opening scene. One such moment is when&nbsp;
Teddy doesn't have a cigarette lighter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.600
As a patient, he's probably not allowed&nbsp;
to have one because it's a dangerous item.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.440
Additionally, the boat's bathroom area&nbsp;
looks suspiciously like the kind of cell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:40.160
where a patient living in a 1950s institution&nbsp;
would be held. But it's the meeting of Chuck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.480
and Teddy that should immediately tip off&nbsp;
viewers that something strange is afoot.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:48.880
Looking back on the film, numerous other clues&nbsp;
lead up to the big twist. It's a movie that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:53.440
rewards multiple viewings, and you'll realize&nbsp;
certain moments come across differently with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.760
knowledge of Teddy's true identity. For instance,&nbsp;
when Teddy and Chuck first arrive on the island,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:02.880
the guards seem to tense up and grip their rifles&nbsp;
a little tighter. Initially, audiences may think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:07.360
there are secrets on the island they need to&nbsp;
protect. In actuality, the guards are nervous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.840
because they know Teddy's one of the patients,&nbsp;
and they don't know if he could snap any second.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:15.360
However, the biggest clue that you might&nbsp;
have missed occurs when the U.S. Marshals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:19.840
are asked to relinquish their guns. There's a&nbsp;
prolonged moment where Chuck fumbles getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.600
his firearm out of its holster. If he&nbsp;
were actually an experienced Marshal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:27.040
he should have no problem getting it&nbsp;
undone. The reason he has an issue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:31.200
is that he's really a doctor and he doesn't&nbsp;
know how to handle a gun properly. At first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:36.640
the scene comes across as amusing, but&nbsp;
it gives up the entire twist right there.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:42.400
With all this in mind, it just goes to show&nbsp;
what a master filmmaker Martin Scorsese is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:47.440
He hid all of these clues in plain sight, yet&nbsp;
most viewers were still taken by surprise.

